Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:49:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 58/63] Panel: back up and restore the universe; Wipe offers a
 backup first

A new Universe row on the control panel:

- Back up now saves the whole universe database to backups\universe-<date>_<time>.sql.gz in the
  server folder (mariadb-dump inside the db container, gzipped). A running server is stopped
  first, so its shutdown save is in the backup, and started again afterwards. The backup only
  counts when the dump's last line says it finished.
- Restore backup... puts the universe back to a backup picked from that folder. The universe as it
  is now is backed up first (-before-restore). A damaged file is caught before anything is
  changed; if the load fails part way, the panel names the safety backup to restore. The server
  starts at the end and its database step brings an older backup up to date.
- Open backups opens the folder. Wipe universe moved to this row and asks whether to back up
  first (-before-wipe).
- The scripts run in the db container are copied in as files with Linux line endings, so nothing
  in them is mangled by Windows PowerShell's quoting.
- backups/ is ignored by git (and was never part of the Docker build).
